---
layout: page.njk
title: "LiDAR scenes — velocity.report"
description: Every published LiDAR scene, placed in the S2 cell that indexes it. Trajectories only — no cameras, no images, no number plates.
---

<style>
  .scenes__title { font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 4vw, 2.3rem); font-weight: 650; letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 0 0 0.35rem; }
  .scenes__sub { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.45; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; opacity: 0.85; max-width: 68ch; }

  .scenes__map { border: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.28); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .scenes__map svg { display: block; }
  #scene-map { height: 520px; border-radius: 3px; }
  #scene-map .leaflet-popup-content { font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .scenes__mapnote { font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.7; margin: 0 0 1.75rem; max-width: 68ch; }

  .scenes__list { display: grid; gap: 1rem; grid-template-columns: 1fr; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  @media (min-width: 760px) { .scenes__list { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }

  .scene-card { border: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.28); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1rem 1.1rem; }
  .scene-card__name { font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 640; margin: 0 0 0.3rem; }
  .scene-card__name a { text-decoration: none; }
  .scene-card__name a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .scene-card__summary { margin: 0 0 0.7rem; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5; opacity: 0.85; }
  .scene-card__cells { margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.7; }
  .scene-card__cells dt { display: inline; opacity: 0.65; }
  .scene-card__cells dd { display: inline; margin: 0 0.9rem 0 0.3rem; font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
  .scene-card__unlocated { margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; line-height: 1.55; opacity: 0.7; }
  .scene-card--recorded { border-style: dashed; }
  .scene-card__tag { font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 500; opacity: 0.6; white-space: nowrap; }

  .scenes__index { font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6; opacity: 0.8; max-width: 68ch; }
  .scenes__index code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
</style>

<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto">
  <h1 class="scenes__title">LiDAR scenes</h1>
  <p class="scenes__sub">
    Each scene is a real recording of a street, published as trajectories: position,
    size, heading and speed, and nothing that could identify anybody. The map marks
    every site the sensor has stood at; click a point to open its survey.
  </p>

  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
        integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />
  <div class="scenes__map">
    <div id="scene-map">
      {# Fallback for a visitor with no JavaScript, and what the page shows
         before the tiles arrive: the self-contained cell diagram, which needs
         no third-party request at all. #}
      {% include "scene-map.svg" %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {# The site list travels in a script block, not an attribute: a place name
     with an apostrophe in it — Fisherman's Wharf — ends a quoted attribute
     early, and the JSON arrives truncated. #}
  <script type="application/json" id="scene-map-data">{{ scenes.sites | dump | safe }}</script>
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
          integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
  <script type="module" src="{{ '/js/scene-map.js' | url }}"></script>
  <p class="scenes__mapnote">
    {{ scenes.published_count }} of the {{ scenes.recorded_count }} sites here have a
    published recording; the rest are places the sensor has been, shown so the map
    answers where it has been rather than only what there is to watch.
    Each point is one recorded site. Click it for the name and, where there is a
    recording, a link to it. Points carry no labels on the map: at this zoom a
    label covers the street it stands on, and the street is the thing worth
    seeing. Every site's S2 level {{ scenes.levels.neighbourhood }} and level
    {{ scenes.levels.area }} tokens are listed with it below.
  </p>

  <ul class="scenes__list">
    {% for site in scenes.sites %}
      <li class="scene-card{% if not site.published %} scene-card--recorded{% endif %}">
        <h2 class="scene-card__name">
          {% if site.page %}<a href="{{ site.page | url }}">{{ site.title }}</a>
          {% else %}{{ site.title }} <span class="scene-card__tag">recorded, not published</span>{% endif %}
        </h2>
        {% if site.summary %}<p class="scene-card__summary">{{ site.summary }}</p>{% endif %}
        {% if site.located %}
          <dl class="scene-card__cells">
            <dt>Site</dt><dd>{{ site.cells.site.display }}</dd>
            <dt>Neighbourhood</dt><dd>{{ site.cells.neighbourhood.display }}</dd>
            <dt>Area</dt><dd>{{ site.cells.area.display }}</dd>
          </dl>
        {% else %}
          <p class="scene-card__unlocated">
            Not on the map: {{ site.position_note }}
          </p>
        {% endif %}
      </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>

  <p class="scenes__index">
    The cells come from <a href="https://s2geometry.io/">S2</a>, which divides the
    globe into a hierarchy of cells and names each one with a token. A token is
    shown here as <code>80858-0f4</code>, hyphenated only to make the shared prefix
    easy to compare; the hyphen carries no meaning and the canonical token is
    <code>808580f4</code>. Every token on this page is derived from the scene's
    recorded position, so a cell and the position it indexes cannot disagree.
  </p>
</section>
